# Coding Style (Keramica Pattern)

Reference project: `keramica`. Match this writing style on HTML/Bootstrap sites. On Next.js/React apps, follow that project's existing patterns instead â€” do not force Keramica HTML structure onto React.

## Stack (static HTML)

- Bootstrap + Font Awesome + Swiper + AOS
- Partials in `app/` (`header.html`, `footer.html`, `loader.html`, modals)
- Load with jQuery: `$("#header").load("app/header.html")` (inline at page bottom or in `main.js`)
- CSS only: `assets/css/style.css` + `assets/css/media.css`
- Never add parallel CSS files (`theme.css`, `custom.css`, etc.)

## HTML structure

```html
<!-- Section banners like Keramica -->
<!-- 
##################################################
#                   Header                       #
##################################################
-->
<header class="header" id="header"></header>

<div class="hero d-md-block d-none">
  <div class="hero-slider position-relative">
    <div class="swiper heroSwiper">
      <div class="swiper-wrapper">
        <div class="swiper-slide position-relative">
          <img ... />
          <div class="overlay"></div>
          <div class="hero-content">
            <span class="hero-slogan">...</span>
            <h1>...</h1>
            <p>...</p>
            <a href="..." class="btn-contact">...</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
```

- Reuse existing classes: `.btn-send`, `.btn-contact`, `.header`, `.hero`, `.hero-content`, `.header-section`
- Keep the project's real nav links â€” do not rename to a third-party template's menu
- Prefer clear comments for major blocks

## CSS (`style.css`)

- TOC + section markers: `/* ========== N. SECTION NAME START/END ========== */`
- `:root` variables at top (`--main-color`, `--second-color`, `--radius`, â€¦)
- Nested CSS (`.header { .navbar { ... } }`, `&:hover`)
- Edit the matching section in place â€” do not append a fighting override block at the end
- Responsive only in `media.css`, grouped by breakpoint (`992px`, `768px`, `576px`)

## JS

- Simple, readable: jQuery IIFE for loader; `DOMContentLoaded` for scroll/header
- Sticky header: toggle `.fixed-top` on `.header` when `scrollY > navHeight`
- Swipers live in `slider.js`
- Prefer small clear functions over clever abstractions

## Change discipline

- Read the file first; continue from what exists
- Small request â†’ small diff
- Restyle by updating existing `.header` / `.hero` / `.btn-send` â€” not new class families
- Brand colors come from that project's `:root` â€” never invent a second palette file

## âŒ Avoid

- Parallel hero/header systems (`hero-renax`, `hero-home` beside `.hero`)
- Extra theme CSS files
- Rewriting menu labels to match a demo template
- Large end-of-file override dumps that override earlier sections

